{"content":[{"c":["OVENS, Tower of the"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Structure in the Jerusalem wall restored by Nehemiah and his workmen after the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.11","r":"Neh.3.11","rawR":"Neh.3.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.11","value":"Neh.3.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.38","r":"Neh.12.38","rawR":"Neh.12.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.38","value":"Neh.12.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:38"},"). Malkijah, son of Harim, and Hasshub, son of Pahath-moab, are named as its builders. The tower was likely a defensive work on the northwest section of the wall, named for its proximity to nearby baking ovens."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"OvensTowerofthe","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Neh 3:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.3.11","rawQueryValue":"Neh.3.11","sourceRefExact":"Neh.3.11"},{"anchorText":"12:38","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.38","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.38","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.38"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"41b0d0a75719a0bd1013ced9f65a3bc36a0ad798fbf009c07d06539df0a7fc85","sourceItemName":"OvensTowerofthe","sourceItemOrder":96,"sourceMember":"Articles/O.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"OvensTowerofthe","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Ovens, Tower of the","title":"Ovens, Tower of the","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}